 ## Overview
-RDLS-SS-DWT+Pred is a lossless volumetric compression transform that combines 3D Discrete Wavelet Transform (DWT) with predictive coding to minimize the entropy of the resulting coefficients [S1]. It operates by applying Reversible Denoising Lifting Steps (RDLS) with step skipping to a 3D-DWT, followed by spatial prediction on the final subbands [S1]. It differs from its sibling [SS-DWT+Pred](6518-ss-dwt-pred.md) by incorporating denoising filters in the lifting steps, though sources indicate that using actual denoising filters yields negligible bitrate improvements over skipping them entirely [S1]. It builds on [Predictive and Differential Coding](4393-predictive-and-differential-coding.md) by applying prediction specifically to the transformed subbands rather than the raw volume data [S1].
+RDLS-SS-DWT+Pred is a lossless volumetric compression transform that combines 3D Discrete Wavelet Transform (DWT) with predictive coding to minimize the entropy of the resulting coefficients [S1]. It operates by applying Reversible Denoising Lifting Steps (RDLS) with step skipping to a 3D-DWT, followed by spatial prediction on the final subbands [S1]. It differs from its sibling [SS-DWT+Pred](6518-ss-dwt-pred.md) by incorporating denoising filters in the lifting steps, though sources indicate that using actual denoising filters yields negligible bitrate improvements over skipping them entirely [S1]. It builds on [Predictive and Differential Coding](4393-predictive-and-differential-coding.md) by applying prediction specifically to the transformed subbands rather than the raw volume data [G].
 
